[E0414] Error: cannot assign to `n` in the value assigned to `n`
    ╭─[ err/86_assignment_order/main.wip:46:9 ]
    │
 45 │     n += {
    │     ┬  
    │     ╰── the place assigned, found before the value
 46 │         n = 10                  // lost: `n` was read first
    │         ┬  
    │         ╰── assigned here
    │ 
    │ Note: `op=` finds its place and reads it before it computes the value, so the value must not change the place
────╯
